  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-4000003953</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP Transboundary Wastewater Management in Attil / Tulkarem Governorate</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on a previous UNDP transboundary waste water pollution control project, this project will target Attil municipality as a replication. It includes infrastructure and a regulatory framework addressing transboundary flows. The current practice in Attil is using cesspits and dumping wastewater into wadi&#x2019;s in surrounding areas. This poses significant public health risks and pollutes natural resources, in particular the shared water aquifer. There is a critical need to establish a comprehensive wastewater management system to safeguard the environment, prevent pollution and manage conflict. The proposed infrastructure consists of a sewage collection system that connects to Israeli treatment facilities. The costs of treatment is directly deducted from PA tax money. To adequately measure this, flowmeters will be installed. In addition, the project intends to build a framework to calculate treatment costs and develop a tariff structure for wastewater.</narrative>
  </description>
